; dn.ext of the Linux packages: the commands that Enter ({ }), Shift-Enter (( )) and Alt-Enter ([ ]) run for a file.
; The mask before the bracket is a list of extensions (as in the filters of the panels, separated by commas) or
; r:<regular expression> for the whole name. In a command ! is the name without the extension, !.! the name with it
; and !\ the directory of the file. DN copies this file into ~/.config/dn at the first start; edit it there
; (Options -> Extension file edit).
;
; xdg-open hands a file to the program that the desktop has for its type.
pdf,djvu,epub,ps{xdg-open "!.!" >/dev/null 2>&1 &}
png,jpg,jpeg,gif,bmp,webp,svg,tif,tiff{xdg-open "!.!" >/dev/null 2>&1 &}
mp3,ogg,oga,flac,wav,m4a,opus{xdg-open "!.!" >/dev/null 2>&1 &}
mp4,mkv,avi,webm,mov,mpg,mpeg{xdg-open "!.!" >/dev/null 2>&1 &}
html,htm,odt,ods,odp,doc,docx,xls,xlsx,ppt,pptx{xdg-open "!.!" >/dev/null 2>&1 &}
r:^(GNUmakefile|[Mm]akefile)$ {make}
